  "query_preview": "..\n(This evening through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1259 PM CDT Thu Sep 3 2026\n\nThis morning's upper air analysis continues to feature an upper-\nlevel ridge centered over the Southeast U.S. This ridge of high\npressure has mostly suppressed convection across the Mid-South\nfor the last several days. Noon temperatures are in the 90s\nareawide with surface dewpoints in the upper 60s to lower 70s.\n\nNBM guidance continues to exhibit a high bias with surface\ndewpoints during peak heating and mixing. Consequently, heat\nindex values have underperformed, remaining mostly just below\nheat advisory criteria. Thus, dewpoints were blended towards the\nNBM 10th and 25th percentiles. A persistence forecast will\ncontinue for the next several days with rain chances remaining\nvery low and mostly confined to north Mississippi. Long range\nensemble data continues to show the upper-level ridge weakening\nslightly into the Labor Day weekend then re-strengthening across\nthe area into next week. Thus, afternoon temperatures will\ncontinue to be mostly in the mid 90s to approaching 100 degrees\neach day.",
